<title>THAILAND: Krung Thai falls on employee protest talk.</title>
<headline>Krung Thai falls on employee protest talk.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Major Thai bank, Krung Thai Bank, fell sharply in active trade on talk in the stock market that the bank's employees may protest later on Wednesday over year-end bonuses, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 0811 GMT, Krung Thai Bank was down 3.00 baht at 56.50 baht and was the most active stock in terms of volume in the bourse.</p>
<p>A bank spokeswoman said she could not confirm the talk in the market but told Reuters: &quot;We heard from some bank staff there may be a protest at 4 p.m. today against possible lower bonuses this year.&quot;</p>
</text>
